_:naeb6bf65a07a48c28692792ae2748c2bb27 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is implicitly projected onto the meme scene, specifically onto the bottom text 'be like vlad', which functions as a direct address to the viewer, inviting them to imagine themselves embodying Vlad's violent actions. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the agent performing the grotesque act described, aligning with the meme's hateful intent to incite a violent, dehumanizing fantasy."@en .
_:naeb6bf65a07a48c28692792ae2748c2bb29 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#outlinedStrokedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target community is individuals who are familiar with or interested in historical memes, particularly those that use exaggerated or distorted historical figures (like Vlad the Impaler) to make politically charged or hateful statements. This includes users who engage with internet humor that relies on shock value, historical inaccuracies, and the projection of violent stereotypes onto religious or ethnic groups. The meme is designed to resonate with audiences who understand the reference to Vlad the Impaler as a brutal historical figure and who may be receptive to or even enjoy the grotesque, hyperbolic, and dehumanizing portrayal of Muslims as barbaric invaders. The target audience likely includes those who consume content that promotes or reinforces harmful stereotypes, particularly those that equate Muslims with violence, sexual depravity, or historical invasions of Europe, and who may be drawn to the meme’s provocative and inflammatory tone."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#verticallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vertically adjacent to"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#toxicity_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hateful"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimensionIndex> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#modallyContradicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#contradicts> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#valuationallyContradicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "valuationally contradicting"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TemporalRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension being temporally related with another in memes, e.g. text adding before/after context to visual material"@en .
